  "semantics": {
    "enable": "CR1.LSEEN bit4 is software RW enable, default0; STABLE bit15 is separate RO status. Only power-on reset resets LSEEN/LSE register. No automatic LSE request is asserted from SDK silence.",
    "mode": "MODE0 requires both pads analog; MODE1 requires PC14 digital input, PC15 can be GPIO.",
    "lock": "CR1.LSELOCK bit5 prevents clearing LSEEN; it is not a configuration lock. Configure all LSE parameters before enable and do not change them while enabled.",
    "write_key": "CR1.KEY bits31:16 must be 0x5A5A. Preserve and write1 CLKCCS/HSECCS/LSECCS bits8/7/6 as explicitly required by the register table.",
    "fault": "ISR.LSEFAIL bit5 indicates startup failure; ISR.LSEFAULT bit7 indicates running failure. Neither is source enable. Running detection needs LSI and checks128 LSE cycles per256 LSI cycles. ICR uses write0 clear; broad flag clearing is outside this cohort.",
    "consumers": "RTC, AWT and UART configuration bus gates do not prove their independent working clocks are idle. MCO SOURCE6 and enabled direct LSE outputs also retain LSE.",
    "gpio": "DIR offset0 controls input/output; SPEED offset8 controls slew. Analog selector offset28. Direct outputs require digital output (ANALOG0/DIR0) and matching AF. This is distinct from SPEED."
  },
